WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.950
You ask a question.

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.330
A word comes back in milliseconds.

3
00:00:05.192 --> 00:00:10.202
This is everything llama.cpp does in
between, slowed way down.

4
00:00:14.265 --> 00:00:16.835
Your message lands on an HTTP worker
thread.

5
00:00:17.245 --> 00:00:18.815
It never touches the model.

6
00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:20.415
It just finds the right handler.

7
00:00:21.792 --> 00:00:27.462
The model's own chat template wraps your
words in special tokens, the way it saw
conversations in training.

8
00:00:28.692 --> 00:00:31.982
Then the tokenizer cuts everything into
sixteen numbers.

9
00:00:32.972 --> 00:00:34.822
Numbers are all the model ever sees.

10
00:00:37.528 --> 00:00:39.618
Your request becomes a task on a queue.

11
00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:42.618
The inference thread picks it up and gives
it a slot:

12
00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:45.118
a lane of its own, with its own memory.

13
00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:51.058
Every tick, every busy slot shares one
batch.

14
00:00:51.488 --> 00:00:58.938
Your sixteen tokens ride along with other
people's chats, and the KV cache keeps
what the model works out, so nothing is
computed twice.

15
00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:02.195
libllama builds the graph:

16
00:01:02.685 --> 00:01:05.155
thirty-two layers of attention and feed-
forward.

17
00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:07.895
Then GGML runs it on the GPU.

18
00:01:09.621 --> 00:01:15.151
Out comes a score for every token in the
vocabulary, more than a hundred and
twenty-eight thousand of them.

19
00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:18.211
The sampler trims the field, and draws
one.

20
00:01:20.737 --> 00:01:23.267
That one token streams back to you.

21
00:01:23.457 --> 00:01:24.547
Then the loop runs again:

22
00:01:24.957 --> 00:01:26.527
one token, every tick.

23
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.670
Until the model says stop.

24
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.150
The slot goes quiet, but it keeps its
memory, so your next message starts warm.

25
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.180
Next time:

26
00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.240
why your second message is faster.
